\pard\b\fs20 Fields of Glory\b0\par
\fs16\par
This folder contains three modified rounds on the same landscape.\par
The landscape is laid out as an open battlefield. The starting positions are higher up and can be fortified at the start of the game to keep the enemy out of your own position. I'm afraid I have to keep repeating it: the rounds are TEAM MELEES. Also, take care not to die; if you are the weaker one in single combat, don't seek it.\par
Details on the objects placed in the landscape and on the game features are in the individual round descriptions (if you have trouble following longer texts attentively, just skip the story and read only the last part).\par
In the Classic version, the player has only a few knights, and the first attack usually decides the game. A cautious war of position is intended here; whoever storms the enemy too recklessly can very easily be wiped out.\par
The Dawn of the Dead version, on the other hand, is more action-packed: here you can reinforce your troops with undead and so keep your knight out of costly fights.\par
The Super Undead version was derived from it. In this round you can upgrade your skeletons. If the player manages to keep their skeletons alive and kill more enemies, the skeletons are upgraded to mages and warriors.\par
In Heavy Fortress, the armies, each led by a king, face each other in fortified castles. There are many relaunches, plenty of flesh to tear and walls to blow up.\par
